    "updated_at": "2021-11-30T14:31:07Z",
    "body": "I have a repo with a handful of submodules in it and just tried switching to starship from a custom zsh prompt and the difference was huge. Here are my timing comparisons:\r\n\r\n- `starship prompt` (1.0.0): 160ms\r\n- `git status --porcelain`: 156ms\r\n- `git status --porcelain  --untracked-files=no --ignore-submodules=dirty`: **1.6ms**\r\n    - (my previous prompt was only concerned with colouring the branch name depending on whether it was dirty or not, and I personally wanted to exclude the above items)\r\n- `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no`: 75.1ms\r\n- `git status --porcelain --ignore-submodules=dirty`: **1.8ms**\r\n- `git status --porcelain --ignore-submodules=untracked`: 75.9ms\r\n\r\ncompared with a [large repo](https://github.com/nixos/nixpkgs) with no submodules:\r\n- `starship prompt`: 161.3ms\r\n- `git status --porcelain --branch`: 160.1ms\r\n- `git status --porcelain`: 67.6ms\r\n- `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no`: **12.6ms**\r\n\r\nI'd very much like my prompt to not be laggy (>50ms or so is pretty intolerable), so it would be nice if:\r\n- `git_status.untracked = \"\"` could cause starship to pass `--untracked-files=no`\r\n    - (and maybe `--ignore-submodules=untracked`)\r\n- `git_status.ahead = \"\" git_status.behind = \"\"` could cause starship to avoid passing `--branch`\r\n-  and it would definitely be useful to have an additional option that passes `--ignore-submodules=dirty`\r\n- consider per-repo/path options and overrides like how `git config oh-my-zsh.hide-dirty` and friends exist",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
